    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Money drain / day (avg per bot)",
      "description": "Per-bot average real-balance depletion over 24h for the selected environment: sum(increase(bot_money_drained_total))/sum(bots_by_env_status). Drain is observed from server-balance deltas and floored at 0, so net-gain windows contribute 0 — this biases the value UPWARD vs true net depletion (it is a burn gauge, not net P&L; AD-2). Divisor is the current bot count, so the average is approximate if the environment was resized mid-window. 'or vector(0)' renders 0 when no bots/series exist.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "currencyVND",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(increase(bot_money_drained_total{environmentId=\"$environmentId\"}[24h])) / sum(bots_by_env_status{environmentId=\"$environmentId\"})) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "drain/day per bot"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Gateway request window vs ceilings (5 min)",
      "description": "GATEWAY_REQUEST_BUDGET. Requests this environment has sent to its gwms gateway in the current 5-minute sliding window (gateway_budget_window_requests), against the app's own hard cap and the three per-tier ceilings — all four read from the box's OWN configuration (gateway_budget_hard_cap, gateway_budget_ceiling{tier}), not from literals in this dashboard, so an operator who uses the documented essential.ceiling=850 escape hatch sees the policy they are actually running. Cloudflare blocks the whole host for that gateway at 1,000 requests / 5 min / source IP and the one observed block outlived an hour. In bot.gateway.budget.mode=observe nothing is paced, so a window above the ceilings means requests really went out at that rate; in enforce, the window sitting AT the ceilings is the budget working — see the queue-depth panel for whether anything is stuck.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 40
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "hard cap"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/ ceiling$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dot",
                  "dash": [
                    2,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "gateway_budget_window_requests{environmentId=\"$environmentId\"}",
          "legendFormat": "requests in window"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "gateway_budget_hard_cap{environmentId=\"$environmentId\"}",
          "legendFormat": "hard cap"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "gateway_budget_ceiling{environmentId=\"$environmentId\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{tier}} ceiling"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Gateway budget queue depth by tier",
      "description": "GATEWAY_REQUEST_BUDGET AD-20. How many requests are WAITING for admission, per tier, in bot.gateway.budget.mode=enforce (in observe this is flat zero by construction). A DEFAULT queue is the design working — registration and drift balance reads are meant to yield. An ESSENTIAL queue means bots that are trying to come up are waiting, which is normal and expected during a large start (AD-18: a 300-bot group is one window, a 3,000-bot group is ten) and is a problem only when it never empties. GatewayBudgetSustainedQueue alerts on exactly that, at 15 minutes of continuous ESSENTIAL queueing.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 48
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
