      "title": "Gateway budget admission wait p95 by tier",
      "description": "GATEWAY_REQUEST_BUDGET AD-20. How long a request waited for admission, p95, per tier. The SLO buckets are 1s / 10s / 60s / 300s / 600s. In observe mode this is ~0 by construction, and gateway_budget_wait_seconds_max < 0.01 is the release check that observe really never parked anything. In enforce, PRIORITIZED rising towards its 10-minute max-wait means reconnects and deposits are being squeezed by a start, and DEFAULT hitting its 30s wait means registration and drift reads are being deferred — both expected during a large start, both worth reading if they persist. ESSENTIAL has no max-wait (0 = unbounded, cancellable) because the window drains by construction, so its p95 is the honest measure of how long a bot waits to come up.",
